What will you do in the role?
This role offers an exciting opportunity for an intermediate-level software engineer to grow their skills in frontend development while also gaining exposure to backend technologies. If you're passionate about building impactful products and enjoy working in a dynamic, collaborative environment, we'd love to hear from you!
What are the key responsibilities of the role?
Develop and maintain frontend features for our web applications, with a primary focus on React components.
Collaborate with product managers and designers to create seamless and intuitive user experiences.
Review code changes and coordinate deployments using CI/CD pipelines.
Assist in architectural decision-making and technical problem resolution.
Take ownership of coding projects from conception to release, ensuring high quality and timely delivery.
What would the ideal candidate be great at?
Technical competence: love coding, able to learn new paradigms quickly and look to continuously improve and find better ways of doing things;
Coding and creating with front-end technologies - HTML, CSS and Javascript on the front-end;
Experience with an OO language such as Python / Ruby and building and querying REST APIs;
Understanding the importance of writing clean code and code testing;
Keeping UI in mind when building and designing;
Teamwork and team spirit; be more motivated by the achievements of the whole team;
Getting up to the front of the bus; get stuck in, execute, generate ideas, have an impact, don’t just sit back and be a passenger;
Attention to detail – you want to make things look good!
Qualifications and experience
At least 3+ years experience in web development;
Strong proficiency in frontend development technologies, including HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with a focus on React;
Experience with object-oriented languages such as Python or Ruby, and building and consuming RESTful APIs;
Familiarity with writing clean, well-tested code and maintaining UI/UX standards;
Ability to work collaboratively in an Agile environment, integrating with backend APIs and contributing to team objectives;
Excellent attention to detail and a passion for crafting visually appealing interfaces.
Experience that would be nice to have (but we’ll trade off if everything else fits)
Familiarity with state management libraries such as Redux;
Familiarity with backend development, particularly with Ruby on Rails or similar frameworks;
Ideally, you are language agnostic and eager to try out new languages as needed;
Experience working in a highly collaborative team;
Start-up experience. Sometimes the earth moves beneath your feet at Prodigy Finance, so you've got to be comfortable with ambiguity, able to wear lots of hats, and adapt easily as we continue to grow.

Experience & Requirements:
University graduate with a three-year degree;
Management experience in a hotel environment preferable;
Must have strong verbal and written communication skills in English, Afrikaans and preferably a 3rd language;
Must have a car and valid driver’s license;
Exceptional organizational and multitasking skills;
Demonstrate integrity, dependability, responsibility, accountability, self-awareness, work ethic, and empathy;
Passion and understanding for CampusKey vision and values;
Excellent in computer skills (Microsoft Word, Outlook and Excel)
Experience in Xero Accounting and Simple Pay
Fully qualified (CA) SA
Critical Competencies for Success
This describes you:
Enthusiastic;
Customer-orientated;
Hard working;
Responsible;
Born motivator and leader.
Do’er
:
Credibility is earned at CampusKey through execution and getting things done.  You are able to get into the details and deliver results under highest expectations on time and quality. Be ready to get hands-on with all aspects of the daily needs. The buck stops with you. Pragmatism and outcomes orientation are valued and lead to wins. Exceptional organizational and multitasking skills. You thrive in a fast-paced environment.
Collaborator
:
There is no room for “I” at CampusKey. Every role and individual is in the organization to serve We. Builds trust across the organization by being a good listener and inclusively soliciting input.  You are open to new and innovative solutions. You must present well and communicate clearly and effectively to upper management and internal departments. You’re willing to adjust course when appropriate new ideas or objections are raised. You love working with people!
