To develop information data-driven insights and apply the elements of cognitive science for planning and policy development, design and create the Artificial Intelligence algorithms capable of learning and making predictions that define machine learning, use data as a tool to make decisions and solve business problems through application of math, business, technology, design thinking, and behavioral sciences, and extract insights from large datasets using analysis, visualization, and mathematical computation and in turn transform those insights into actionable business decisions. The person appointed to this position will be stationed in the Market Integrity and Decision Sciences Division and report to the Departmental Head: Market Surveillance and Data Analysis.
Key Performance Areas
Develops predictive modelling and trend analysis tools that anticipate the needs and provide real-time solutions to meet those needs;
Acts as the organisation’s Data Analytics expert;
