Purpose Statement
To manage end-to-end audit preparation processes, while ensuring adherence to established timelines.
Minimum Requirements
B.Com/ B Comm (Hons) with 8 years post articles (SAICA signed-off) experience;
CA (SA), ACCA of CIA will be an added advantage;
Previous work experience with the AGSA would be an added advantage;
At least 5 years external and internal audit management experience;
Proven track record of preparing audit files that are IFRS, PFMA and Companies Act compliant annual financial statements;
Proven track record of designing and implementing systems of control, ultimately leading to a positive audit outcome;
Proven track record of leading and liason for AGSA audits;
Extensive knowledge of IFRS; PFMA; Companies Act and other public sector legislation;
Ability to operate in a highly pressurised environment, with quick turnaround times;
Ability to deal with complex matters and provide integrated solutions;
Experience with Draftworx or Caseware in preparing working papers and annual financial statements
Duties and Responsibilities
Manage end-to-end audit preparation processes, while ensuring adherence to established timelines.
Document end-to-end audit preparation processes, including month-end financial accounting procedures for training and capacitation of the financial accounting business unit and ultimate implementation.
Maintain accurate and organized records (manual and electronic) of account balance and transaction working papers and documentation following best practice and established audit file preparation standards and protocols.
Assist the SABS with pre-audit preparation and project management.
Manage and guide with reconciliation of sub-ledger control accounts to GL accounts.
Manage and guide with reconciliation of GL accounts to account balances as well as reconciliations to working papers.
Ensure alignment of electronic and manual audit file to approved and published annual financial statements before submission to relevant treasury, shareholders, AGSA and SNG Grant Thornton.
Liaise with external auditors during the audit process and provide necessary support for the audit of financial statements;
Analysis and updating of audit workpapers and ensuring consistent treatment with prior year audited working papers or adherence to new accounting requirements.
Prepare accounting, finance and operational personnel for the audit process.
Assist with liaison to auditors and key stakeholders to provide audit support through each phase of the audit, working along with the SFA.
Ensure that audit requests provided to auditors are accurate, complete, and have been reviewed and approved prior to submission to auditors.
Assist in addressing all findings raised by the AGSA, SNG Grant Thornton and internal audit department.
Assist IFRS specialist with identifying and applying intercompany reconciliations, ensuring consistent treatment from the prior year.
Provide valuable insights and recommendations based on audit findings to improve financial controls, operational efficiency, and risk management, post the audit.
Resolve general accounting and operational issues and disputes, escalating as required or coordinating with various business units

Vestas Mediterranean (MED) is a Region within Vestas Wind Systems, covering wind markets in South Europe, Africa and the Middle East, each corresponding to MED Sub-Regions.
The position is primarily for South Africa, dealing mainly with transactions, corporate matters, compliance and general legal matters but may also involve, when needed, support to the rest of MED Sub-regions.
The Legal Department provides legal advice in relation to the sale and services transactions which include preparing, negotiating and drafting the transactions documents as well as agreements with the different stakeholders to reach the established business goals.
Responsibilities
Reporting to the Director of Legal South/East MED, the key tasks are the following:
Prepare, negotiate, draft and finalize transactional documents (EPCs, Turbine Sales Agreements, Service Agreements, Procurement Agreements) as well as subsequent ancillary documents under such contracts, i.e. parent documentation, lender direct agreements, escrow agreements, NDAs, etc.;
Ensure and provide continuous legal support on issues arising after transactional documents are signed and during the execution phase, including disputes and potential litigation;
Provide legal counselling to Management with respect to legal and regulatory matters pertaining to the wind energy sector;
Partner closely with other department stakeholders to identify issues of risk facing the organization and propose and drive solutions to address them;
Monitor national laws and regulations pertaining to the company's business, including those relating to Compliance;
Ensure that the relevant corporate governance is timely and properly applied along the closing of each transaction;
Take care of corporate matters;
Ensure, in coordination with the team, that:
the review process and management of commercial opportunities is applied in compliance with the internal mandates obtained by the relevant functions;
the different tasks for the purpose of the realization of each project are properly allocated and accepted by all stakeholders of the contracting process; and deadlines are met,
Develop and implement good contracting practices, including, providing legal awareness training and creating templates and contract policies;
Coordinate and manage tasks assigned to external legal advisors, especially litigation.
Qualifications
LLB in South Africa, or equivalent; LLM in business, commercial or energy law desirable;
Admitted Attorney in South Africa;
Solid legal educational background handling/analyzing complex transactions especially relating to construction industry or large-scale projects;
Experience in legal, commercial and contracting functions with Original Equipment Manufacturers in the RES sector or preferably in the wind energy industry (or other significant experience with handling large-scale international construction, industrial equipment tools, automotive, etc.).
Competencies
Efficient negotiation skills and capability to deal with intensive negotiation sessions,
Strong ethical principles and compliance focus,
Ability to effectively influence and communicate within all levels of a global organization, as well as third parties,
Ability to work proactively and collaboratively as the primary legal point of contact and to prioritize among different urgent matters,
High organizational skills,
Ability to work in time sensitive environments,
Ability to examine complex problems and apply legal principles, facts and precedents to recommend adoption of an effective, practical and proper course of action,
Appetite/strong interest for business-related matters and ability to connect the legal dimension with value creation impact,
General curiosity for renewables, environment, sustainable solutions and their associated products,
Proven commitment to continuous self-improvement,
Occasional travelling may be needed, based on company needs and goals,
Commercial mindset and interest in learning more about commercial and technical issues,
Innovative and independent mindset, but with demonstrated stakeholder management skills and experience working in a multinational, matrixed organization,
Computer literate (MS Office),
Fluency: English, including legal and business terminology.
