Purpose of the Job:
To provide and manage the activities of the Business Centre Complaints and Queries team, which include but not limited to the following: handling of complaints from multiple sources, redirecting of complaints to external regulatory authorities and internal FSCA divisions in accordance with relevant protocols and management of the debarment register. The person appointed to this position will report to the Departmental Head.
Key Performance Areas:
Oversee and manage the complaints and query resolution unit within the Business Centre;
Assist with the development, implementation and maintenance of the appropriate internal policies;
Implement and over the implementation of the Complaints and Queries Framework;
Engage with internal and external stakeholders with regards to the activities of the Unit;
Manage the human resources of the team effectively and efficiently (train, monitor, lead, development and maintenance of performance standards for the team);
Assist in managing the department’s business plan and budget in line with FSCA guidelines;
Attend to administrative and managerial responsibilities of the department as directed by the Departmental Head;
Manage the processes of referral of matters that do not fall within the scope of the FSCA to external stakeholders;
Prepare monthly trend analyses reports on matters handled by the Unit;
Manage, monitor and update the register of debarred representatives; and
Engage with key internal and external stakeholders to facilitate the closure of various matters and ensure adherence to service level agreements.
Requirements
A Bachelor’s Degree in law or Commerce. The candidate must have proven relevant and practical experience of at least 5 years within a financial services industry. A good understanding of the overall mandate of the FSCA and the various financial sector laws is required.

Job Description
The Operations Department has a vacancy for 5 x Junior Inspector to conduct inspection of products and equipment according to standard protocols as prescribed through PPECB’s legislative mandate and for the developmental opportunities for some of our seasonal employees to gain additional competencies within the 24-month period of the programme.
The purpose of the programme is to allow the incumbent sufficient time for product exposure; training; assessment; and soft skills. During the 24-month period the selected delegates will be supported with a dedicated training plan and supervision by the region. The exposure and training will include:
Technical competencies to the value of a minimum of 50 credits based on regional requirements;
TITAN 2.0 ® competency;
Product theoretical course (AETP module);
I-thrive (e.g., managing my time; dealing with conflict; etc.);
Additional soft-skills courses to promote professional skills; and
Additional courses to prepare for the new world of work (NWOW)
Depending on the regional needs; delegates of the programme may have the opportunity to take part in Relief Duty to receive exposure on additional products and will then be supported with accommodation and S&T allowance during such placements.
Areas of Responsibilities:
Inspect and certify perishable products;
Inspect the handling, storage and transport of perishable products;
Ensure the correct application of quality management systems, BMS procedures and working instructions;
Perform administrative tasks;
Build and maintain good relations with PPECB clients;
Communicate with various clients on own specific task and outcome of decisions;
Participate in the relief duty roster;
Accept the responsibility of continuous self-improvement in their area of responsibility
Job Requirements
Areas of Responsibilities:
National Diploma in an agricultural or food science disciplines.
National Certificate: Perishable Produce Export Technology (AETP)would be advantageous.
Practical experience, theoretical knowledge/exposure or competency in citrus
Good verbal and written communication skills.
Computer literate.
The ability to work independently and / or with minimum supervision.
A valid code 08 drivers license and own reliable vehicle is a requirement for doing the job
Additionally, the following criteria will be reviewed:
Relevant Service history to the job in question at the PPECB
Competency records (verified by L&D)
Performance records at the PPECB
Disciplinary records during their service/contract at the PPECB
Please note: preference will be given to applicants who have not participated in the 24-month programme before.

Description
The Role
Pele Green Energy is seeking a talented, highly motivated, and self-driven Electrical Engineer. The engineer will report to the Head of Operations. The Engineer will provide engineering support to the Project Development, Asset Management and Constuction Managment teams across the portfolio of projects with the Group, during development, construction and operational phases of the projects.
Job Responsibilities
Technical Enginering (Primary)
Detailed analysis of electrical engineering LV (LV ≤ 1 000 V), MV (MV ≤ 33 kV) and HV (132kV) design drawings (equipment, layouts and configurations,);
Analyse grid integration studies, Bill of Materials, technical reports, engineering designs and drawings, and yield studies to provide inputs to the development cycles of projects
Strong and sound knowledge of electrical distribution designs, including primary equipment (transformers, HV/MV cable networks, Switchgear , etc) and Protection & Control systems applicable to IPP infrastructure.
Operate computer-assisted engineering and design software and equipment to perform engineering tasks (AutoCAD, PV*Syst, Wind*Syst / WAsP).
Perform detailed calculations to compute and establish construction and installation standards and specifications;
Interpret Load flow studies and Protection study reports.
Sound Knowledge on Secondary and Automation applications.
Analysis of electrical schematic drawings and single line diagrams;
•Management of switchgear, transformer, AC breaker and specialist equipment manufacturers and/or suppliers (verification of specification conformation and factory acceptance testing);
Coordinate/oversight of manufacturing, construction, installation, maintenance, support, documentation and testing activities to ensure compliance with specifications, codes, regulatory and customer reequipments;
Prepare specifications for purchase of materials and equipment;
Develop budgets, estimating labour, material and construction costs;
Cost evaluation of electrical engineering scope of work, including equipment and construction costs;
Compile data and write reports regarding existing and potential engineering studies and projects;
Review of Communications network designs for Power Plants (on-site) and Head Office based data center environments;
Collect field surveys and study maps, graphs, diagrams and other data to identify and correct system problems;
Full knowledge and co-ordination of South African Grid Code performance, both during testing and commissioning, as well as operational lifetime
Compiling all necessary technical documentation and liaising with Grid stakeholders, Eskom Control Centers, Single Byers Office, etc
Reporting to project stakeholders
Operations
Review of operations and maintenance report and data from the operator;
Recommend improvements of preventative and corrective maintenance and make recommendations of predictive maintenance;
Review of expert engineering report and data from the external service providers;
Plant/asset performance supervision- ensuring that the plant preforms according to the PPA and the relevant contractual performance ratios;
Intergate condition monitoring and optimisation- improving generation and revenue as consequence;
Plant (re) commissioning - ensuring that all systems and components of the plant are designed, installed, tested, operated, and maintained according to the operation requirements;
Technical Rick mitigation in accordance with the SANS standards and applicable electrical standards during the implementation of Engineering Retrofits, Engineering changes, and plant optimisation activities;
Technical recommendation to ensure safety maintenance and operability practices and efficient utilisation of systems space and equipment spacing;
Re-powering and upgrades – ensuring that all additional upgrades required or needed to be done on the plant are done to the satisfaction of the Sponsors and Lenders and all necessary reporting is done;
Monitoring install/retrofit – ensuring that all necessary installation or retrofitting of equipment by the O&M Contractor or external contractors is within acceptable standards and does not hinder the performance of the plant and daily production;
Plant design review – ensuring that all new designs are compliant to various international standards and are satisfactory to the requirements of the Sponsors and Lenders;
Grid code compliance – ensuring that SPV is fully compliant with the requirements of the South African grid code and necessary studies are completed;
Harmonic and fault levels studies – overview and monitoring of all the studies and tests needed to ensure that SPV is compliant according to the Grid Code and Power Quality Guidelines requirements for Harmonics and fault levels;
Engineering and Construction
Technical review of complete designs, equipment sizing, drawings, specifications, data sheets, and other supplementary design work in the degree of detail necessary to enable the client's inspections to clearly determine the engineering, procurement manufacturing, and construction work requirements;
Review of status of engineering progress and deliverables;
Tracking engineering change requests, initial operation, testing, and remedying of defects;
Receipt and approval of the EPC final dossier;
Ensure that installations and applications are in line with the technical specifications and safety standards.
Construction Management participation with the Project implementation team;
Technical reviews and assistance with Technical Due Diligence procedures.
Technical advice and assistance to Project Development
Assisting in the scope of work for the Owner’s Technical Specifications ;
Assisting in conducting technical due diligence, including review and update of technical aspects of project documents such as the Grid impact study, Hydrology report, Geotechnical report, Technology assessment, Energy Forecast, Performance ratios, NPV, Load Profiles, PVSyst model files, Resource assessments, Topographical surveys, Environmental Impact Assessments, Codes and Standards, etc.
Planning and executing engineering activities needed for any RFPs related to Services, Supply, and Works: preparation of the technical package to be provided to Procurement Function within the Organization, Bids Technical evaluation and ranking.
Requirements
BEng or BSc (Eng) in Electrical Mechatronic or Electronic Engineering (other streams can be motivated)
Minimum 5 years’ experience in engineering design and/or project engineering (within the renewable energy industry)
Ability to work across multiple work streams, projects, and contracts
People and Team Management
Sound Understanding and knowledge of database systems, SCADA integration etc would be advantageous;
Proficient in MS Word, MS Projects, MS Power Point and MS Excel
Has Drivers’ License and own car – site visits are required
Commercial competency
Budget management
Risk management

RESPONSIBILITIES:
Manage the procurement process from initiation to completion of payment;
Act as a point of contact between the company and suppliers & identify potential suppliers based on project requirements;
Manage supplier evaluation and selection;
Negotiate contracts, terms and deadlines with vendors and suppliers;
Manage the complete contract life cycle from Creation, Collaboration, Signing, Tracking, Renewal and Closure;
Receive feedback and monitor the supplier lead time and quality of services provided;
Monitor price fluctuations of goods and vendor pricing and work out a strategy to ensure best pricing and quality to be supplied to FlySafair;
Liaise actively with the Technical department heads to understand the needs across the Technical department;
Review requests for Quotations (RFQs) and monitor all delivery timelines are met and to ensure a >98% OTIF;
Manage accurate records for all procurement activities;
Prepare financial and quality Audits;
Accurately track and report key functional metrics;
Thoroughly examine and test existing contracts to ensure maximum contract value on agreed contracts;
Together with the Warehouse manager, monitor Consignment stock and report back to suppliers and Management;
Provide input into the Annual Budget and future capacity requirements;
Responsible for the overall Performance of Contract Obligations and the effectiveness of the Contract;
Monitor and report on the total Value of Contract and ensure price competiveness;
Oversee the compliance rate and is accountable for the Purchase Order accuracy;
Manage the full procurement team and their performance.
REQUIREMENTS:
Grade 12;
Degree in Finance, Logistics, Supply Chain Management, Business Administration or Equivalent;
5+ years Procurement experience of which, must include 3 years managerial experience;
Proven experience of previous Contract Management;
Proficient in Procurement procedures and best practices;
Proficient knowledge of inventory and inventory controls;
Aviation experience (preferred);
Knowledge of SAM AMO system (advantageous);
Qlickview experience (Advantageous).
PERSONAL ATTRIBUTES:
Excellent communication skills both written and verbal;
Aptitude in decision-making and working with numbers;
Strong leadership
Organisational, multitasking, and problem-solving skills;
Critical thinker;
Deadline driven;
Immaculate time keeping.
